{"title":"Optometrist Roadmap","role":"Optometrist","summary":"An Optometrist is an eye-care professional involved in examining vision and ocular health, identifying refractive errors, prescribing corrective lenses where legally permitted, detecting common eye conditions, providing vision rehabilitation, and referring patients to ophthalmologists when medical or surgical intervention is required.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Optometry (B.Optom)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Optometrist is an eye-care professional involved in examining vision and ocular health, identifying refractive errors, prescribing corrective lenses where legally permitted, detecting common eye conditions, providing vision rehabilitation, and referring patients to ophthalmologists when medical or surgical intervention is required."},{"type":"p","text":"Core areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Comprehensive eye examinations"},{"text":"Refraction and prescription"},{"text":"Contact lenses"},{"text":"Binocular vision"},{"text":"Pediatric optometry"},{"text":"Low-vision care"},{"text":"Ocular disease screening"},{"text":"Myopia management"},{"text":"Optical dispensing"},{"text":"Community eye care"},{"text":"Pre- and post-operative vision support"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Scope note","text":"The exact professional scope, registration requirements, prescribing authority, and permitted clinical procedures vary by jurisdiction and applicable regulations."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Primary Focus","Career Outcome"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Anatomy, physiology, optics, basic sciences"},{"text":"Strong foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Optometric examination and refraction"},{"text":"Core clinical skills"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Binocular vi